  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Physical Description
    
    A Nightshelf grimoire of the **Grend Blood-Arts**, bound in volcanic glass covers the color of old blood and fitted with ribs of ancestor-bone that click audibly when opened. The pages are thin as ice-film but warm to the touch, inscribed in silver ink visible only in absolute darkness. The tome's contents include rituals the Nightshelf have not performed in three generations, techniques for reading the pressure-memory of the deep, and methods for binding orca-blood to stone. Its third chapter describes pre-consolidation suppression techniques that predate the unified **☽Silv-glaciere☽** school of practice by an indeterminate period — a detail whose implications for the history of **Hush☽ Twilight** have not, to my knowledge, been adequately explored.
    
    ## Provenance and Damage
    
    The Lantern was recovered from **The Whispered Shrift~**, a contested Nightshelf tunnel network, during the **Orca Incursion**. It bears two distinct wounds. The first is physical: during the **Mbra∴silentiu** — the contested-waters conflagration that collapsed the old factional hierarchies — a surface-dweller's spear-thrust cracked the spine, leaving a diagonal fracture across the back cover. The second is not physical. When **Breach (ice-screamed)** erupted at Terrace Momiou, the tome was locked in a cedar chest at **The Thewsed Slew~**, a desecrated Nightshelf site. The ice-scream left a localized Hush☽ Twilight effect across the spine — a zone where the pages no longer hold memory and readers report losing time. Floe-master **☽'Sanctsevotis'Tier** has documented three variant transcriptions from the same page taken on consecutive days. The passages shift between readings. I note this without explanation because I have none.
    
    ## Chain of Theft
    
    The Lantern has been stolen four times. All four thieves are deceased and known only by trade-names:
    
    | Thief | Fate |
    |---|---|
    | **Jark Rankzule** | Deceased; circumstances unrecorded |
    | **Gnarkzund Zaith** | Orca raider of the Incursion era; died at Aurora Stack during the casting of Grulkzul Omega Strike |
    | **Rend Kzulrora** | Scarred orca raider; survived the Lantern but bears other wounds |
    | **Krathund Gnurl** | Carried it kelp-wrapped on his harness until a catastrophic blood-working dispersed him across the frozen deep near the Still Pools |
    
    None read past the third chapter. An earlier version of this record lists five thefts; the discrepancy is unresolved, though the four named holders are consistent across all sources.
    
    Krathund Gnurl's end is documented in orca pressure-song: the blood-working **Grulkzul Omega Strike** consumed the pod-bond connecting him to his packmate **Deep Maw Krixizak** and scattered the Lantern along with his other stolen artifacts into the water. How the tome was subsequently recovered and secured at the Thewsed Slew~ is not recorded.
    
    ## Current Status
    
    The Lantern now rests at **Umbra∴go**, a Nightshelf memorial site, behind shadow-steel bars. The Nightshelf built the memorial around it but refuse to retrieve the tome itself. Veiled inquiries about the blood-to-stone binding arts described in its pages have surfaced near Umbra∴go — questions posed in wrong proverbs, drawing Fire Keeper scrutiny and warnings from Nightshelf elders. Someone is reading what the tome teaches without opening it, or someone has already read enough.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
